{
  "name": "Start",
  "comment": "A path-backed image reads nothing at the set, so a strict mismatch does NOT\nfail here — it is deferred to byte-materialization (first content load). The\nset itself is clean; the throw-at-load is covered by the C#\nLazyPathHandleTests.BytesAsync_StrictKindMismatch_ThrowsAtLoad. Requires the\ncommitted photo.png fixture.",
